Always run **desktop + mobile** on at least Home and one blog post with code.

## Budgets (gatekeeper)

- Desktop Accessibility: **100** on core pages
- Mobile Accessibility: **≥ 95**
- Blog posts with code: aim **≥ 95** after CodeBlock/Search fixes (was 89 when unnamed)

Failing SEO audits like `link-text` (generic „Weiterlesen“) still matter for a11y of link purpose — fix even if Accessibility score is 100.

## Extract failures (do not load full JSON into context)

```bash
node -e "
const r=require('./.a11y-reports/<page>/report.json');
const a11y=new Set((r.categories.accessibility?.auditRefs||[]).map(x=>x.id));
console.log('a11y', Math.round((r.categories.accessibility?.score||0)*100));
for (const a of Object.values(r.audits).filter(a=>a.score!=null && a.score<1 && a11y.has(a.id))) {
  console.log(JSON.stringify({id:a.id,title:a.title,n:(a.details?.items||[]).length}));
}
"
```

Structure check: write `structure-<page>.json` via `evaluate_script` (h1 count, heading list, skips, orphan inputs).

## Known hotspots in this codebase

| Issue | Where |
|-------|--------|
| Icon-only controls need `aria-label` | `Search.tsx`, `CodeBlock.tsx` |
| Nested checkbox in button breaks `label`/`button-name` | Avoid DaisyUI swap+checkbox pattern for copy |
| Card/tech titles under section `h2` → use `h3` | `Card` `titleAs`, `TechCard`, homepage sections |
| Generic „Weiterlesen“ | `BlogCard` → `aria-label` with post title |
| Redundant page/textBlock titles | `CmsPageContent` + `ContentTextBlock` `hideTitle` |
| Footer tap size | `min-h-11` / padding on footer links |

## Reporting

For durable, multi-page audits: produce a **Canvas** (`.canvas.tsx`) with scores, prioritized findings (P0–P3), WCAG refs, file paths, and a fix backlog. Raw reports live in `.a11y-reports/` (gitignored).

## Automation (preferred direction)

When adding CI:

1. **PR:** axe-core (or Lighthouse) against local `next build && next start` — fail on P0 (`button-name`, `label`, missing names).
2. **Post-deploy / nightly:** Lighthouse CI against production URLs with budgets above; upload JSON/HTML artifacts.
3. Page list = table above (+ sample post with code).

Do not treat Lighthouse 100 as “done” without checking outline and named controls on mobile.

## After fixes

Re-run Lighthouse on affected pages (desktop + mobile) before calling the work done. Release via git-flow (`develop` → `main`) when the user asks.
